      "env": {
          "DOCKER_IMAGE": "<your desired Docker image>",
          "DOCKER_NETWORK": "<a name for the Docker network (e.g., cypress_network)>",
          "SCREENSHOT_FOLDER": "<the folder location for saving screenshots>"
      }
   }
   ```

   Here, `baseUrl` is the URL for the application under test (usually hosted in the Docker container), and `env` defines variables needed for dockerization and screenshot management.

   b. Add the following code to your main Cypress configuration file, `cypress.json`, to utilize the multi-config setup:

   ```javascript
   {
     "testFiles": "**/*(.cy|.spec).js",
     "experimentalDocker": true,
     "screenshotsFolder": "<base folder path for screenshots>",
     "video": false, // set to true if you want video recordings as well
     "pluginsFile": "cypress/plugins/index.js",
     "configFile": "cypress.config.js",
